# Moqesh admin dashboard: example Caddy snippet (reverse proxy + TLS).
#
# Exposes the dashboard (port 5000 of the moqesh-ai container) on its own TLS subdomain,
# SEPARATE from the public honeypot and the sensors subdomain. The gate is the Moqesh
# login (cookie session); Caddy only acts as reverse proxy + TLS.
#
# Requisitos:
#   1) DNS:  A  moqesh-admin.example.com  ->  <your server's IP>
#   2) moqesh-ai reachable by your Caddy (same Docker network) and listening on :5000
#      (add your proxy's external network to the `moqesh` service; see docker-compose.vps.yml).
#   3) In the compose file: MOQESH_COOKIE_SECURE=true and a fixed admin password
#      (or read ONCE from the container log).
#
# Add this block to your Caddyfile and reload Caddy. Adjust the domain and, if your Caddy runs in
# a container, the service name (moqesh-ai) to match your network.

moqesh-admin.example.com {
	encode gzip zstd
	reverse_proxy moqesh-ai:5000
}
